---
title: Person lifecycle driven by producer events (account state in OpenIAM)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> Enabled : hire<br/>saveUser + groups/roles/orgs

    state Active {
        direction LR
        Enabled --> Disabled : status sets a hold<br/>(e.g. compliance non_compliant,<br/>training overdue)
        Disabled --> Disabled : another hold added,<br/>or one of several cleared
        Disabled --> Enabled : last hold cleared
        Enabled --> Enabled : update<br/>(fields, group/role/org lists)
    }

    Active --> Leave : leave<br/>leave-of-absence (optionally scheduled)
    Leave --> Leave : status changes recorded,<br/>no enable/disable while on leave
    Leave --> Enabled : return, no holds
    Leave --> Disabled : return, holds still active

    Active --> Terminated : terminate<br/>(effective_date schedules it)<br/>granted access removed
    Leave --> Terminated : terminate

    Terminated --> Terminated : hire / update / return refused<br/>rehire is manual

    note right of Terminated
        Every transition queues AD instructions
        (enable / disable / add_member / remove_member)
        for the other site. No AD connection.
    end note
